<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Round 6 of the localisation sweep (2026-08-28).

    Every string here was previously a hardcoded English literal sitting in a
    Composable, so it rendered in English in all 33 languages. The audit that
    found them looks at every user-visible sink — Text(), label=, title=,
    placeholder=, contentDescription=, supportingText=, actionLabel= and
    Toast.makeText — not just Text(), because a linter that only knows one
    shape reports "all accounted for" while the other shapes leak.

    Deliberately NOT resourced, and why:
      - "OSHI"                          brand name, 5 sites
      - emoji-only labels               nothing to translate
      - "buf:", "1280x720 @ 30fps"      developer overlay in VideoCallScreen
      - "© OpenStreetMap contributors"  attribution must appear verbatim
-->
